<title>USA: Duff puts Philippines obligations on rating watch.</title>
<headline>Duff puts Philippines obligations on rating watch.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Monday it placed the foreign currency obligations of the Republic of the Philippines on rating watch-up.</p>
<p>Duff said it currently rates the foreign currency obligations of the Philipines double-B.</p>
<p>Duff said the move recognizes the substantial progress the Philippines has achieved toward macroeconomic stabilization and sustainable growth. Duff also upgraded the status of the rating outlook to positive from stable.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
